# Efficiency allowlist — read by crates/marion-testsupport/tests/three_axis (run: scripts/three-axis.sh).
#
# Format: `path:item  one-line reason`. A finding not listed here fails the check; an entry nothing
# matches fails it too, so a fix deletes its line. THIS LIST ONLY SHRINKS. The perf waves are
# replacing these timer-driven waits with event-driven ones (poll(2)/kqueue, condvars, pipes);
# a bounded one-shot wait with a clear deadline may stay, and says so.

# --- bounded one-shot waits with a clear deadline (every idle poll is gone, perf-wave2) ---------
crates/marion-supervisor/src/serve.rs:run_conn_writer  blocks in recv(); the try_recv loop only drains what is queued after the connection departed, then ends (perf-wave1 74d9b38)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/rpc.rs:Driver::settle_until  bounded: waits on the reader/inbox condvar; try_wait is the one non-event check, once per LIVENESS_TICK (2 s) while a node is live, for a server that died with its stdout still held
crates/marion-supervisor/src/rpc.rs:LIVENESS_TICK  bounded: the safety bound on a condvar wait (2 s), never the ordinary path — see Driver::settle_until
crates/marion-supervisor/src/acp_child.rs:prompt_session  bounded: the held-inbox wait blocks on the shared driver's condvar (rpc::Driver::wait_event); try_wait once per wake or LIVENESS_TICK (2 s)


crates/marion-supervisor/src/detach.rs:DIAL_POLL  bounded: ensure_supervisor re-dials every 5 ms, once per client start, until a supervisor answers or READY_DEADLINE; a stillborn stage 3 releases its flock, which no file watch reports, so this wait cannot be a watch alone
crates/marion-supervisor/src/detach.rs:ensure_supervisor_within  bounded: the DIAL_POLL loop, one-shot at client start, ended by the dial or READY_DEADLINE (see DIAL_POLL for why it is not a watch)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/socket.rs:acquire_within  bounded: a stage 3 that finds the lock held re-asks every 2 ms until the holder binds or START_DEADLINE; a holder dying before it binds only releases a flock, which no file watch reports
crates/marion-supervisor/src/native_bootstrap.rs:exchange_native_claim  bounded: one claim exchange under LAUNCH_RESULT_TIMEOUT, then reset to blocking
crates/marion-supervisor/src/bin/marion.rs:SupervisorSession::request_detach_all  bounded: one request/response under SUPERVISOR_REPLY_WAIT
crates/marion-supervisor/src/wake.rs:poll_until  bounded one-shot wait: the one sleep-until-deadline loop, for a child's exit or a file nothing can wake on; every caller passes its own budget (ready file, INTERRUPT_GRACE, SUPERVISOR_EXIT_WAIT)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/kill.rs:observe_dead  bounded one-shot wait: reads a killed process's state with backoff (1 ms doubling to OBSERVE_PAUSE_MAX) until it is gone or the kill deadline passes, so the kill confirmation is earned; never runs idle

# --- home-polish (2026-09-27): the event-driven home loop ---------------------------------------
crates/marion-supervisor/src/home/session.rs:TICK  bounded: the home screen wakes on it only while something on the tab moves (a running node's elapsed time, a harness being checked); an idle screen has no timeout at all
crates/marion-supervisor/src/home/session.rs:Session::reports  not a poll: drains the side threads' channel once the wake pipe says a report arrived; never loops on a timer
crates/marion-supervisor/src/client_auth.rs:hello  bounded: one read timeout per connection, the handshake deadline HELLO_WAIT (5 s), cleared once the hello is answered; a silent listener would otherwise hang the client for ever
